IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sumlma-member`

-- Superannuation (Unclaimed Money and Lost Members) Act 1999 ss 15A and 20B -- the unclaimed money days and scheduled
-- statement days the Commissioner has specified, and with them the day by which my fund must pay my money to the ATO. A
-- module beside sumlma-member.l4 in the same baseline; it IMPORTs that module and changes none of it.
--
-- SEAT: the member (as in sumlma-member.l4) -- "My money became unclaimed (or inactive, or lost) on this day, or the ATO told my
-- fund on this day that I am a former temporary resident. By when must my fund pay it to the ATO?"
--
-- Sources:
--   the Act, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/C2004A00518.txt, ss 15A, 17(1), 20B, 20F(1), 20QD(1), 24E(1);
--   Unclaimed Money Days and Scheduled Statement Days, F2009L04037 (made 16 October 2009 under s 15A), as deposited at
--   ../../../unclaimed-money-days-and-scheduled-statement-days/registers/source-bundle/F2009L04037.txt;
--   Temporary Residents' Superannuation Measure - Scheduled Statement Days 2009 year and onwards, F2009L01210 (made 25 March
--   2009 under s 20B), as deposited at
--   ../../../temporary-residents-superannuation-measure-scheduled-statement-days-2009/registers/source-bundle/F2009L01210.txt;
--   the Superannuation (Unclaimed Money and Lost Members) Regulations 2019 (deposited beside the Act), which identify no later
--   day for s 20F(1)(c).

§ `ss 15A, 20B -- the days the Commissioner has set, and by when my fund must pay`

-- s 15A: "The Commissioner may, by legislative instrument, specify: (a) days as being unclaimed money days for the purposes of
-- this Part and Parts 3B and 4A; and (b) for each unclaimed money day--a day (the scheduled statement day) by the end of which a
-- statement required by this Part or Part 3B or 4A, in relation to the unclaimed money day, is to be given".
-- F2009L04037: "the unclaimed money days shall be: 31 December, and 30 June in each year." "the scheduled statement days shall
-- be: for an unclaimed money day being 31 December of any year - 30 April of the following year, and for an unclaimed money day
-- being 30 June of any year - 31 October of that year."
-- ss 16(1), 20QB(1), 24C(1): the statement is of the unclaimed money, inactive low-balance accounts or lost member accounts "as
-- at the end of the day"; ss 17(1), 20QD(1), 24E(1): the amount is "due and payable at the end of the scheduled statement day
-- for the unclaimed money day". So money that qualifies on a day is reported for the first unclaimed money day on or after it.
-- The instrument was made in 2009 when s 15A spoke of Part 3 alone; it is read as specifying the days s 15A now uses for Parts
-- 3B and 4A as well (NOTES.md finding 16).
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the first unclaimed money day on or after` MEANS
    IF `the day` AT MOST Date 30 6 (DATE_YEAR `the day`)
    THEN Date 30 6 (DATE_YEAR `the day`)
    ELSE Date 31 12 (DATE_YEAR `the day`)

GIVEN `the unclaimed money day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the scheduled statement day for` MEANS
    IF DATE_MONTH `the unclaimed money day` EQUALS 6
    THEN Date 31 10 (DATE_YEAR `the unclaimed money day`)
    ELSE Date 30 4 (DATE_YEAR `the unclaimed money day` PLUS 1)

-- s 20B: "The Commissioner may, by legislative instrument, specify days (scheduled statement days) by the end of which
-- statements required by this Part are to be given". F2009L01210: "the first scheduled statement shall be 15 June 2009, and each
-- subsequent scheduled statement day shall be 31 October and 30 April."
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the next Part 3A scheduled statement day after` MEANS
    IF `the day` LESS THAN Date 15 6 2009
    THEN Date 15 6 2009
    ELSE IF `the day` LESS THAN Date 30 4 (DATE_YEAR `the day`)
         THEN Date 30 4 (DATE_YEAR `the day`)
         ELSE IF `the day` LESS THAN Date 31 10 (DATE_YEAR `the day`)
              THEN Date 31 10 (DATE_YEAR `the day`)
              ELSE Date 30 4 (DATE_YEAR `the day` PLUS 1)

DECLARE `The day my fund must pay the ATO by` IS ONE OF
    `by the end of the day` HAS `the due day` IS A DATE
    `no day: my fund may pay the Commissioner under s 22 but is not required to`
    `not covered: my money qualified before 28 October 2009, when the unclaimed money days now in force were registered, and the earlier days are not deposited`

@export By when must my super fund pay my money to the ATO, with the days the Commissioner has set worked out?
GIVEN `why` IS A `Why my fund pays the Commissioner` @desc Why your money is going to the Commissioner: unclaimed money, an inactive low-balance account, a lost member account, a former temporary resident notice, an eligible rollover fund account, or a voluntary payment by your fund
      `the day my money qualified` IS A DATE @desc For unclaimed money, inactive low-balance and lost member accounts: the day your money first became unclaimed money, or your account first became an inactive low-balance or lost member account (ignored otherwise)
      `the day of the notice` IS A DATE @desc For a former temporary resident: the day the Commissioner gave your fund the s 20C notice about you (ignored otherwise)
      `my ERF balance was under $6,000 on 1 June 2021` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For an eligible rollover fund account: whether its balance at the end of 1 June 2021 was less than $6,000 (ignored otherwise)
GIVETH A `The day my fund must pay the ATO by`
`By when must my fund pay the ATO, with the days worked out` MEANS
    IF     (    `why` EQUALS `my money is unclaimed money (s 17(1))`
             OR `why` EQUALS `my account is an inactive low-balance account (s 20QD(1))`
             OR `why` EQUALS `my account is a lost member account (s 24E(1))`)
       AND `the day my money qualified` LESS THAN Date 28 10 2009
    THEN `not covered: my money qualified before 28 October 2009, when the unclaimed money days now in force were registered, and the earlier days are not deposited`
    ELSE CONSIDER `By when must my fund pay the Commissioner` `why` `the scheduled statement day` `the day of the notice` `the next day` `the day after that` FALSE `the day of the notice` `my ERF balance was under $6,000 on 1 June 2021`
         WHEN `by the end of` `d` THEN `by the end of the day` `d`
         OTHERWISE `no day: my fund may pay the Commissioner under s 22 but is not required to`
    WHERE
        `the scheduled statement day` MEANS `the scheduled statement day for` (`the first unclaimed money day on or after` `the day my money qualified`)
        `the next day` MEANS `the next Part 3A scheduled statement day after` `the day of the notice`
        `the day after that` MEANS `the next Part 3A scheduled statement day after` `the next day`
